  "strongest_argument": "The native TreeView eliminates an entire defect class the current design is structurally prone to: full-DOM-teardown rendering plus hand-rolled hit-testing (fact 8's swallowed-click bug is not a fluke, it's the natural failure mode of hand-rolled hover strips over reflowing DOM). No amount of test-suite investment removes that risk in the hand-rolled version; a TreeView removes it by construction because the workbench owns rendering and hit-testing.",
